# PH25 (2026-09-19): dependency-manifest scan exemptions. Scope = Maven +
# npm manifests only (see the "Dependency vulnerability scan" step in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml), NOT the container image — image exemptions
# live in deploy/security/.trivyignore.
#
# Review EVERY entry when the referenced dependency is upgraded: an entry
# that outlives its rationale is a silently disabled gate (#895).
#
# Suppressed findings are printed on every run via --show-suppressed, so
# this file hides an advisory from the exit code, never from the log.
#
# ===========================================================================
# SECTION 1 — NOT REACHABLE. Version is left alone on purpose; rationale is
# expected to stay true until the dependency is next bumped.
# ===========================================================================
#
# org.bouncycastle:bcprov-jdk18on 1.78.1 (backend/persistence-postgres/
# pom.xml:33-36, pulled in for Argon2PasswordEncoder; it carries an explicit
# <version> there instead of inheriting the Boot BOM, which is why it is
# resolvable even when the BOM chain is not). None of the three advisories
# sits on a code path this project reaches:
#   - CVE-2025-14813 GOSTCTR block handling — GOST ciphers are not used;
#   - CVE-2026-8763 PKIX name-constraints bypass — no certificate-path
#     validation is performed with BouncyCastle here;
#   - CVE-2026-13506 lazy ASN.1 sequence DoS — no untrusted DER parsing.
# The fixes land in 1.80.2 / 1.84 / 1.85, i.e. a version jump outside a
# dependency-audit change; bump it in a dedicated task and DROP these rows.
CVE-2025-14813
CVE-2026-8763
CVE-2026-13506
#
# ===========================================================================
# SECTION 2 — TRACKED BASELINE. Real HIGH/CRITICAL advisories against
# versions this repo actually resolves to, recorded so the gate can land and
# start catching NEW ones. Each row names the live tracker that removes it —
# a row whose tracker has landed is a bug, not a baseline.
#
# Reachability is judged per row below and is NOT what puts a row here; the
# tracker is. (Section 1 rows, by contrast, are here because they are
# unreachable and no bump is planned.)
# ===========================================================================
#
# (org.postgresql:postgresql had three rows here until 2026-09-19. Its
# tracker landed: #973 -> PR #975 pinned the driver to 42.7.12 in
# backend/pom.xml's dependencyManagement, so develop no longer resolves the
# vulnerable 42.7.5 and the rows were deleted rather than left to rot.)
#
# (org.apache.kafka:kafka-clients and spring-boot-starter-actuator had three rows
# here until 2026-09-20. Their trackers diverged: #980 -> PR #1017 moved
# spring-boot.version 3.4.5 -> 3.5.16, whose BOM resolves kafka-clients 3.9.2 (the
# fix for CVE-2026-35554), while the actuator rows' named tracker (dependabot
# PR #87, 3.4.5 -> 4.1.1) was instead closed unmerged on 2026-09-20. The rows'
# own DROP condition — "the resulting Boot line is >= 3.5.12 / 4.0.4" — was
# already met by PR #1017 (3.5.16) and met again by PR #1088 (4.1.1,
# backend/pom.xml:33), so develop no longer resolves either vulnerable version.
# PR #1027 deleted CVE-2026-35554 but not the two actuator rows, which by then
# suppressed nothing (no actuator entry appears in the Security gate's suppressed
# list) yet still withheld the blocking power for a future regression, under a
# mangled copy of their rationale. They are removed here rather than left to rot:
# a row that outlives its rationale is a silently disabled gate for that CVE.)
